# Template — `infra/deploy.sh` substitutes {{PUBLIC_DOMAIN}} and, only when a
# second domain is passed to it, appends this block into the same
# /etc/caddy/Caddyfile the private API's block (`infra/Caddyfile`) lives in.
# Not consumed directly.
#
# Reverse-proxies to `apps/public-api` on 127.0.0.1:4320
# (`apps/public-api/src/config.ts`'s `DEFAULT_PORT`) — the private API's
# equivalent block proxies to 4319. Caddy gets its own Let's Encrypt
# certificate for this domain too, independent of the private one's.

{{PUBLIC_DOMAIN}} {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:4320
}
